/*!
    \page soniclogging-index.html
    \title Sonic Logging

    Sonic Logging is the logging library for SonicDE. It installs a Qt message
    handler that gives every executable its own log file, sends messages to
    journald where it runs, and gives SonicDE code a small logging API. Logs
    stay usable without systemd.

    \list
    \li \l Sonic::Logging: install() sets up the handler for a program.
    \li \l SONIC_LOGGING_COMPONENT(): declares a binary's component, which
        sonicDebug(), sonicInfo(), sonicWarning(), sonicCritical() and
        sonicFatal() log under.
    \endlist

    \section1 Using the Module

    \section2 Building with CMake

    Use the \c find_package() command to locate the SonicLogging package and
    link against its target:

    \badcode
    find_package(SonicLogging REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(mytarget PRIVATE Sonic::Logging)
    \endcode

    \section1 API Reference

    \list
        \li \l{Sonic Logging C++ Classes}
    \endlist
*/
